'''Squirrels''' are small, passive [[creatures]] commonly found in [[Forest|forests]] that can be processed for their [[Clean Squirrel Carcass|meat]], [[Fresh Squirrel Hide|hide]], and [[Squirrel#Production|more]].

==Acquisition==

Squirrels spawn individually as entities in all forest [[terrain]] at all times of year, as well as within [[Squirrel Cache|Squirrel Caches]] that populate forest and [[grassland]] terrain.

Squirrels can be caught via right click by [[Hearthling|Hearthlings]] that have learned [[Hunting]]. Alternatively, squirrels found within Squirrel Caches can instead be obtained, without [[Skills|Skill]] requirements, as an item. One squirrel takes up two slots of [[inventory]] until wrung and flayed.

The [[quality]] of a caught squirrel is hardcapped by a Hearthling's [[Survival]].

== Behavior ==
Squirrels will attempt to flee when approached by a Hearthling, whether they are being chased or not. The speed at which squirrels run is variable, but they can almost always be caught by a Hearthling at normal running speed.

Squirrels can be [[Combat|attacked]], but have no [[Combat moves|Combat Moves]] with which to defend themselves and will simply continue to flee until defeated.

In addition to Hearthlings, squirrels can also be hunted by [[Fox|foxes]], which will chase, attack, and inevitably overpower the squirrel, leading to its demise. The fox will immediately lose interest once the squirrel has been killed, leaving it to be freely obtained by any nearby Hearthling.

== Production ==
When used an ingredient, squirrel meat serves as an accessible source of [[Attributes#Intelligence|Intelligence]] [[FEP|FEPs]].
